\begin_layout Section
Quantitative Analysis
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
This section evaluates the policy and benchmark counterfactuals around the self-employment calibration.
 The key object is not only the overall entrepreneurship rate,
 but the composition of entrepreneurship between nonemployer self-employment and employer entrepreneurship,
 together with the change in average entrepreneurial scale.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
Unemployment insurance ladder
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
 The first benchmark experiment lowers unemployment insurance while keeping the benchmark self-employment calibration fixed.
 The main pattern is monotone:
 lower UI raises entrepreneurship,
 shifts entrepreneurs toward self-employment,
 and reduces average firm scale.
 This is the central necessity-entrepreneurship result in the new benchmark branch.
\end_layout

